WEBVTT

00:55:56.833 --> 00:56:00.684
You know, that is giving you meaning
because it is in itself meaningful.

00:56:00.708 --> 00:56:01.976
AG: Yeah.

00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:03.434
Yeah, for me, that resonates.

00:56:03.458 --> 00:56:05.726
And so I guess what I say to students is,

00:56:05.750 --> 00:56:08.768
when they say, "I want to find
a job I'm passionate about,"

00:56:08.792 --> 00:56:10.268
or "I want to love my work."

00:56:10.292 --> 00:56:12.726
That to me is something
you can look forward to

00:56:12.750 --> 00:56:14.268
10, 20 years down the road

00:56:14.292 --> 00:56:16.851
after you've figured out
where you find meaning

00:56:16.875 --> 00:56:19.809
and what kind of
contribution you can make.

00:56:19.833 --> 00:56:23.143
But I don't feel like
there's an easy answer

00:56:23.167 --> 00:56:25.976
to your question,
which is a really interesting one.

00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:28.143
Why would you leave something you love?

00:56:28.167 --> 00:56:31.601
This is another paradox point though,
that you yourself have made, right?